---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Display from '../components/Display.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Installer from '../components/Installer.astro';
---
<Base title="Hearthboard Ink · A quieter kind of screen" description="Install Hearthboard Ink on the supported Seeed EE04 ESP32-S3 7.5-inch e-paper DIY kit. Board compatibility, browser flashing, Wi-Fi setup, and recovery.">
<section class="container page-hero"><div><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Displays</a><span>/</span><span>Ink</span></div><div class="eyebrow">A QUIETER KIND OF SCREEN</div><h1>Hearthboard<br />Ink<span style="color:#7c8f67">.</span></h1><p class="lead">Your plans, weather, and little reminders. A paper-like display that makes space for what matters.</p><div class="intro-badges"><span class="pill">ESP32-S3</span><span class="pill">7.5″ monochrome</span><span class="pill">Early access</span></div><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="#installer">Open the installer <Icon name="usb" size={18}/></a><a class="text-link" href="/docs/ink-setup/">Setup guide <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div></div><div class="product-art ink-art"><Display kind="ink"/><span class="art-tag">ILLUSTRATIVE DASHBOARD · SAMPLE CONTENT</span></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">START WITH THE RIGHT BOARD</div><h2>Same chip doesn't mean same display.</h2></div></div><p class="prose">Panel drivers and wiring vary, even between ESP32-S3 devices. Match the exact board below before installing.</p><div class="board-grid"><article class="board-option active"><span class="pill">Initial release target</span><h3>TRMNL 7.5″ DIY kit</h3><p>Seeed XIAO ePaper Display Board EE04 with XIAO ESP32-S3 Plus. 800 × 480, monochrome. This is the first hardware target.</p></article><article class="board-option"><span class="pill">Not available yet</span><h3>reTerminal E1001</h3><p>A future target. Don't install the EE04 image on this board; it needs its own hardware verification and release.</p></article><article class="board-option"><span class="pill">Not available yet</span><h3>reTerminal E1002</h3><p>A future color display target. A shared ESP32 chip does not make the monochrome firmware compatible.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container two-col"><div><div class="eyebrow">MAKE IT HEARTHBOARD</div><h2 style="margin-top:15px">From USB to<br />your everyday.</h2><ol class="setup-steps"><li><strong>Connect your board</strong>Use a computer and a data-capable USB cable. Close any serial monitor. If the board is asleep, press one of its buttons first.</li><li><strong>Install the firmware</strong>Check your exact board, then use the installer. Keep USB connected until it completes.</li><li><strong>Let the screen guide you</strong>Scan the Wi-Fi QR on the panel, join Hearthboard-XXXX, then enter your 2.4 GHz home Wi-Fi.</li><li><strong>Pair and make it yours</strong>Rejoin home Wi-Fi on your iPhone. Open Hearthboard, select the display, and confirm the matching pairing digits.</li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/docs/ink-setup/">The complete walkthrough <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><Installer/></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container two-col"><div><h2>Good to know.</h2><ul class="checklist"><li><Icon name="check" size={17}/> Full panel refreshes flash black and white. That's normal.</li><li><Icon name="check" size={17}/> Battery operation sleeps between check-ins; edits wait until the board wakes.</li><li><Icon name="check" size={17}/> USB power keeps the board connected for quicker changes.</li><li><Icon name="check" size={17}/> Calendar, reminders, chores, and photos need a paired Hearthboard iPad feed host.</li></ul></div><div><table class="spec-table"><caption class="eyebrow" style="text-align:left;padding-bottom:12px">INITIAL HARDWARE TARGET</caption><tbody><tr><th>Board</th><td>Seeed EE04 / XIAO ESP32-S3 Plus</td></tr><tr><th>Display</th><td>7.5″ · 800 × 480 · black & white</td></tr><tr><th>Memory</th><td>16 MB flash · 8 MB PSRAM</td></tr><tr><th>Wi-Fi</th><td>2.4 GHz</td></tr><tr><th>First installation</th><td>USB from a supported desktop browser</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="small">Check the exact kit label, not just the screen size.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="container help-banner" style="margin-top:45px"><div><h2>Need a fresh start?</h2><p>Wi-Fi resets, sleeping boards, and getting back to stock firmware.</p></div><a class="button outline" href="/docs/ink-recovery/">Ink recovery guide <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></section>
</Base>
